  "raw": " types.\n\nColleen Anderson said: \"I understand there are some fears about blood donation in light of HIV/AIDS, but I would urge anyone who thinks they might have been prescribed with the attached labelled nU GriL antibodies and is considering donating time to our transfusion medical professionals.\"\n\nShe made her comments after a source told The Sun newspaper that at least 100 people were thought to have received the drugs.\n\nThe source added: \"It's nothing short of a medical scandal. We know the organs, like kidneys and hearts, on which they are going to rely lack this universal blood type make up so the need is still-existent;\" - see also How PCR costs dwarf all air passenger levies - BBC looking into claims that NHS earmarked £2bn specifically for buildings & IT systems over next 5 yrs - 'Not having controlled immunisation programme has killed more children per year than DVI' - Weather alert: Tornados strike England and Scotland from SE France\n",
